"program_narrative": "PORTADD is a batch program that creates new portfolio master records from a sequential input file. It opens the indexed portfolio master file (PORTFOLIO-FILE, random access by PORT-KEY) for update and the sequential INPUT-FILE for reading. The main loop reads one input record at a time into the portfolio record layout (copybook PORTFLIO) until end of file. Each record is validated: a blank portfolio ID, a blank client name or a status other than 'A' (active) rejects the record and counts it as an error. A valid record is stamped with today's date as its creation and last-maintenance date and written to the portfolio master; the file status then classifies the outcome as added, duplicate key (status '22') or write error. At the end it closes both files, displays the added, duplicate and error counts, and passes WS-RETURN-CODE to the operating system (0 normally, 8 when a file could not be opened). Error conditions handled: file open failure, invalid input data, duplicate key and other write errors.",
"paragraphs": [
  {"name": "0000-MAIN", "section": null, "paragraph_id": "SYS-PORTFOLIO-001-FIL-0067-PAR-0001", "section_id": null, "line_range": [76, 85],
   "pseudocode": [
     "-- Main control: initialise, add records until input is exhausted, terminate",
     "CALL 1000-initialize",
     "WHILE NOT end_of_file DO  -- PERFORM 2000-PROCESS UNTIL END-OF-FILE (tested before each pass)",
     "  CALL 2000-process",
